userNameAttribute setting is ignored



Environment


Spring boot starter:


active directory spring boot starter (tested with 2.2.4 and 2.2.5-SNAPSHOT)



OS Type: Windows


Java version:


11



Summary

The user name attribute setting is ignored, the value of the "name" attribute is used instead.
Reproduce steps

Set the user name attribute in application.properties using:
spring.security.oauth2.client.provider.azure-oauth-provider.user-name-attribute=upn
or:
spring.security.oauth2.client.provider.azure-oauth-provider.userNameAttribute=upn
Fetch the username as explained in the demo code in this repository:
    @GetMapping("/")
    public String index(Model model, OAuth2AuthenticationToken authentication) {
        model.addAttribute("userName", authentication.getName());

Expected Results

Value of the upn attribute.
Actual Results

The value of the name attribute is returned.
When setting breakpoints, AADOAuth2UserService.java the userNameAttrName value is null, causing DEFAULT_USERNAME_ATTR_NAME to be returned instead:
    private String getUserNameAttrName(OAuth2UserRequest userRequest) {
        String userNameAttrName = userRequest.getClientRegistration()
                .getProviderDetails().getUserInfoEndpoint().getUserNameAttributeName();
        if (StringUtils.isEmpty(userNameAttrName)) {
            userNameAttrName = DEFAULT_USERNAME_ATTR_NAME;
        }

        return userNameAttrName;
    }



Hi, @dvut . The userNameAttribute value is contained in providers during construction of a client registration. So if you want to set spring.security.oauth2.client.provider.azure-oauth-provider.user-name-attribute, then you need to set this as well.

spring.security.oauth2.client.registration.azure.provider=azure-oauth-provider

Otherwise the default provider azure will be chosen which contains the default userNameAttribute vaule of "name".
Besides, the attribute userNameAttribute cannot be obtained using the API we give in  the sample
    @GetMapping("/")
    public String index(Model model, OAuth2AuthenticationToken authentication) {
        model.addAttribute("userName", authentication.getName());

authentication.getName() is used to obtain the user name, which is different user name attribute.

