Ok everyone, I finally have this solved.  I have learned way more about the Flame engine internals than I had ever planned on, lol.  To summarise:
The issue has nothing to do with what it seemed like on the surface.  In short, the _reAddChildren() method is the culprit, because it recalls _addChild onto itself.  No big deal, but after the game and all components have been loaded and mounted, the component class that is called from the FlameGame.mount, is already mounted, thus isMounted AND isLoaded are true, BUT because _reAddChildren() clears the children, child.isMounted is false.  Thus we simply need to check for if (isMounted && !child.isMounted) { and everything works including the tests.



