🌟Feature request: Allow passing default value/custom store for inputValue into combobox builder


Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.
At the moment I struggle to change the initial value of an input field without user intervention. For example I am using combobox from melt-ui, and I am storing user's data in local storage. When the user visit the page, I want to update the inputValue based on the value I retrieve from local storage. At the moment it seems to be impossible
Describe the solution you'd like
Either the builder accept a new args, defaultInputValue for passing a string of default value, or the builder accept a user provider inputValue store in the args for createCombobox builder.
Describe alternatives you've considered
Passing the store from parent to combobox, and code the update logic there myself, but it is just very messy.
Additional context
Add any other context or screenshots about the feature request here.


This is currently possible, you can use the defaultSelected prop:
const {
		elements: { menu, input, option, label },
		states: { open, inputValue, touchedInput, selected },
		helpers: { isSelected },
	} = createCombobox<Manga>({
		forceVisible: true,
		defaultSelected: {
			value: userData.value,
			label: userData.label,
		},
});

If you need to update it after the page has loaded, you can use the store returned from the builder:
const {
		elements: { menu, input, option, label },
		states: { open, inputValue, touchedInput, selected },
		helpers: { isSelected },
	} = createCombobox<Manga>({
		forceVisible: true,
		defaultSelected: {
			value: userData.value,
			label: userData.label,
		},
});

// just an example, this could be trigger by a function call or whatever
$: if (userData) {
	selected.set({ value: userData.value, label: userData.label ?? userData.value })
}



