Expected result
Unless the user interacts with the Player UI, such as pressing the pause button, the playbackState parameter should reflect the proper reason, in this case when the current track ends it should be  Player.PLAY_WHEN_READY_CHANGE_REASON_END_OF_MEDIA_ITEM.
I use this to determine what to do if the player only wants the current track played, or to continue to play the next track.
@Override
public void onPlayWhenReadyChanged(boolean playWhenReady, int playbackState) {
	Player player = BibleAudioPlayer.this.player;
	if (player == null) return;

	boolean continuousIsChecked = continuousToggleSwitch.isChecked();
	boolean repeatIsChecked = repeatToggleSwitch.isChecked();
	if (playbackState == Player.PLAY_WHEN_READY_CHANGE_REASON_END_OF_MEDIA_ITEM) {
		if (!(continuousIsChecked || repeatIsChecked)) {
			player.seekTo(0);
		} else {
			player.play();
		}
	}
}

